## psc/psource.pengu — `SourceFile`: bytes inmutables, índice de líneas y hash.
##
## `SourceFile` es la única copia del texto de un archivo dentro de PSC. Guarda
## los bytes **sin BOM** (CRLF preservado), un índice de inicios de línea y el
## SHA-256 de los bytes **originales** (BOM/CRLF incluidos).
##
## ## Convenciones
## - `line` y `col` son 1-indexed.
## - `col` es una columna de **byte**, no de codepoint. Coincide con
##   `std.sourcemap` y con el lexer; el LSP convierte a UTF-16 en el borde.
## - `\n` empieza una línea nueva. En un par `\r\n`, el `\r` sigue contando para
##   los offsets, pero `line_text` lo excluye.
## - Los offsets son relativos a `text` (después de quitar el BOM). Para obtener
##   el offset en el archivo original: `offset + bom_len`.
##
## ## Ejemplo
## ```pengu
## import psc.source
##
## var f as SourceFile is calling SourceFile.from_text with "a.pengu", "hola\nmundo\n"
## defer banish f
## var p as sourcemap.Position is calling f.position_at with 6
## # p.line == 2, p.col == 1
## ```
##
## ## Memoria
## `banish f` libera `path`, `text`, `line_starts` y `sha256`.

import std.builder
import std.digest
import std.sourcemap
import std.spark

import psc.span as pspan

## Primer byte de un BOM UTF-8.
const SOURCE_BOM_0 as int is 0xEF

## Segundo byte de un BOM UTF-8.
const SOURCE_BOM_1 as int is 0xBB

## Tercer byte de un BOM UTF-8.
const SOURCE_BOM_2 as int is 0xBF

## Byte de line feed.
const SOURCE_LF as int is 10

## Byte de carriage return.
const SOURCE_CR as int is 13

## Por qué falló una lectura de archivo.
omen SourceErrorKind:
    ## El archivo no se pudo leer (no existe, permisos, E/S).
    SrcRead
    ## La ruta no es utilizable como archivo.
    SrcInvalidPath

## Error de carga de un archivo. No es un diagnóstico léxico: no hay pspan.
##
## ## Memoria
## `banish error` libera `path` y `message`.
rune SourceError derive Nexus:
    ## Categoría del fallo.
    kind as SourceErrorKind
    ## Ruta solicitada.
    path as string
    ## Mensaje legible.
    message as string

## Construye un `SourceError` con copias propias de `path` y `message`.
##
## ## Memoria
## Devuelve un valor owned; liberar con `banish`.
weave source_error with kind as SourceErrorKind, path as string, message as string into SourceError:
    var p as string is "{path}"
    var m as string is "{message}"
    return with kind is kind, path is p, message is m

## Convierte los 32 bytes de un SHA-256 a hex minúsculas.
##
## `std.digest.sha256_hex` usa `ord (raw at i)`, que en 3.0.3 asigna un string
## por byte y filtra. Este helper usa `bytes of` y un builder, sin temporales.
##
## ## Memoria
## Devuelve un `string` owned; liberar con `banish`.
weave sha256_hex_of with raw_hash as string into string:
    var sb as StringBuilder is calling StringBuilder.new
    defer banish sb
    var raw_bytes as ref to frozen byte is bytes of raw_hash
    var i as int is 0
    var n as int is raw_hash length
    while i < n:
        var b as int is (raw_bytes at i) to int
        var hi as int is (b >> 4) & 0x0F
        var lo as int is b & 0x0F
        calling sb.append_char with (calling nibble_char with hi)
        calling sb.append_char with (calling nibble_char with lo)
        set i is i + 1
    return calling sb.finish

## Carácter hex de un nibble (0-15).
##
## ## Memoria
## O(1), no asigna.
weave nibble_char with n as int into char:
    if n < 10:
        return (48 + n) to char
    return (87 + n) to char

## Un archivo fuente inmutable.
##
## ## Memoria
## `banish file` libera `path`, `text`, `line_starts` y `sha256`.
rune SourceFile derive Nexus:
    ## Ruta lógica usada en diagnósticos (la que pasó el llamador).
    path as string
    ## Bytes sin BOM; CRLF preservado.
    text as string
    ## Offset del primer byte de cada línea. Siempre empieza en 0.
    line_starts as list of int
    ## SHA-256 hex de los bytes originales (incluye BOM y CRLF).
    sha256 as string
    ## Bytes de BOM eliminados al principio.
    bom_len as int
    ## Longitud original del archivo en bytes.
    raw_len as int

enchanting SourceFile:
    ## Construye un `SourceFile` desde bytes crudos.
    ##
    ## Quita todos los BOM iniciales, conserva CRLF y calcula el SHA-256 de
    ## `raw` (antes de quitar el BOM).
    ##
    ## ## Parámetros
    ## - `path`: ruta lógica; se copia.
    ## - `raw`: contenido binario; se copia.
    ##
    ## ## Memoria
    ## Asigna `text`, `line_starts`, `sha256` y `path`. Liberar con `banish`.
    weave ritual from_bytes with path as string, raw as string into SourceFile:
        var n as int is raw length
        var scan as int is 0
        var rb as ref to frozen byte is bytes of raw
        while scan + 2 < n:
            if ((rb at scan) to int) != SOURCE_BOM_0:
                break
            if ((rb at (scan + 1)) to int) != SOURCE_BOM_1:
                break
            if ((rb at (scan + 2)) to int) != SOURCE_BOM_2:
                break
            set scan is scan + 3
        var tlen as int is n - scan
        var text as string is raw at scan to n
        var raw_hash as string is calling digest.sha256_raw with raw
        var hash as string is calling sha256_hex_of with raw_hash
        banish raw_hash
        var starts as list of int is list of int
        calling starts.push with 0
        var i as int is 0
        var tb as ref to frozen byte is bytes of text
        while i < tlen:
            if ((tb at i) to int) == SOURCE_LF:
                calling starts.push with i + 1
            set i is i + 1
        var p as string is "{path}"
        return with path is p, text is text, line_starts is starts, sha256 is hash, bom_len is scan, raw_len is n

    ## Alias de `from_bytes` para texto ya en memoria (LSP, tests).
    ##
    ## ## Memoria
    ## Igual que `from_bytes`.
    weave ritual from_text with path as string, text as string into SourceFile:
        return calling SourceFile.from_bytes with path, text

    # ------------------------------------------------------------------
    # Consultas básicas
    # ------------------------------------------------------------------

    ## Ruta lógica del archivo (prestada).
    weave get_path into string:
        return self->path

    ## Texto sin BOM (prestado).
    weave get_text into string:
        return self->text

    ## Longitud del texto en bytes.
    weave byte_len into int:
        var t as string is self->text
        return t length

    ## Número de líneas. Un archivo vacío tiene una línea vacía.
    weave line_count into int:
        return self->line_starts.len

    ## SHA-256 hex de los bytes originales (prestado).
    weave get_sha256 into string:
        return self->sha256

    ## Bytes de BOM eliminados.
    weave get_bom_len into int:
        return self->bom_len

    ## Longitud original del archivo.
    weave get_raw_len into int:
        return self->raw_len

    ## Convierte un offset del texto sin BOM al offset del archivo original.
    weave file_offset with offset as int into int:
        return offset + self->bom_len

    ## `true` cuando `offset` está en `[0, byte_len]`.
    weave is_valid_offset with offset as int into bool:
        return offset >= 0 and offset <= (calling self.byte_len)

    # ------------------------------------------------------------------
    # Offset <-> (line, col)
    # ------------------------------------------------------------------

    ## Convierte un offset de byte a `(line, col)` 1-indexed.
    ##
    ## Los offsets fuera de rango se clampan. `position_at(byte_len)` es la
    ## posición justo después del último byte.
    ##
    ## ## Memoria
    ## O(log líneas), no asigna.
    weave position_at with offset as int into sourcemap.Position:
        var off as int is offset
        if off < 0:
            set off is 0
        var n as int is (calling self.byte_len)
        if off > n:
            set off is n
        var lo as int is 0
        var hi as int is self->line_starts.len - 1
        while lo < hi:
            var mid as int is (lo + hi + 1) / 2
            if (self->line_starts at mid) <= off:
                set lo is mid
            else:
                set hi is mid - 1
        var start as int is self->line_starts at lo
        return with line is (lo + 1), col is (off - start + 1)

    ## Convierte `(line, col)` 1-indexed a un offset de byte.
    ##
    ## Panica si la posición no existe. Los usos internos de PSC prefieren
    ## `span_at`, que clampa.
    ##
    ## ## Memoria
    ## O(1), no asigna.
    weave offset_of with line as int, col as int into int:
        if line < 1 or line > self->line_starts.len:
            calling spark.panic with "SourceFile.offset_of: line out of range"
        if col < 1:
            calling spark.panic with "SourceFile.offset_of: column must be >= 1"
        var start as int is self->line_starts at (line - 1)
        var off as int is start + col - 1
        if line < self->line_starts.len:
            var next_start as int is self->line_starts at line
            if off >= next_start:
                calling spark.panic with "SourceFile.offset_of: column past end of line"
        else:
            if off > (calling self.byte_len):
                calling spark.panic with "SourceFile.offset_of: column past end of source"
        return off

    ## Texto de una línea (1-indexed), sin `\n` ni `\r\n`.
    ##
    ## ## Retorno
    ## Un `string` owned; liberar con `banish`.
    ##
    ## ## Memoria
    ## Asigna la longitud de la línea.
    weave line_text with line as int into string:
        if line < 1 or line > self->line_starts.len:
            calling spark.panic with "SourceFile.line_text: line out of range"
        var start as int is self->line_starts at (line - 1)
        var end as int is calling self._line_end_offset with line
        return self->text at start to end

    ## Rango que cubre una línea sin su terminador.
    ##
    ## ## Memoria
    ## Asigna un temporal para medir la línea; devuelve un valor.
    weave line_span with line as int into pspan.ByteSpan:
        var start as int is self->line_starts at (line - 1)
        var end as int is calling self._line_end_offset with line
        return with start is start, end is end

    ## Posición del final del archivo.
    ##
    ## ## Memoria
    ## O(log líneas), no asigna.
    weave eof_position into sourcemap.Position:
        return calling self.position_at with (calling self.byte_len)

    # ------------------------------------------------------------------
    # Spans y slicing
    # ------------------------------------------------------------------

    ## Convierte un `ByteSpan` en el `ByteSpan` normalizado del archivo.
    ##
    ## ## Memoria
    ## O(1), no asigna.
    weave span_at with start as int, end as int into pspan.ByteSpan:
        var s as pspan.ByteSpan is with start is start, end is end
        return calling pspan.span_clamp with s, (calling self.byte_len)

    ## Copia el texto del pspan.
    ##
    ## ## Retorno
    ## Un `string` owned; liberar con `banish`.
    ##
    ## ## Memoria
    ## Asigna la longitud del pspan.
    weave slice with s as pspan.ByteSpan into string:
        var c as pspan.ByteSpan is calling pspan.span_clamp with s, (calling self.byte_len)
        return self->text at c.start to c.end

    ## Byte en `offset` como entero, o `-1` fuera de rango.
    ##
    ## ## Memoria
    ## O(1), no asigna.
    weave byte_at with offset as int into int:
        var n as int is (calling self.byte_len)
        if offset < 0 or offset >= n:
            return -1
        var raw as ref to frozen byte is bytes of self->text
        return (raw at offset) to int

    # ------------------------------------------------------------------
    # Helpers privados
    # ------------------------------------------------------------------

    ## Offset del final del texto de una línea, sin `\n` ni `\r`.
    weave _line_end_offset with line as int into int:
        var start as int is self->line_starts at (line - 1)
        var end as int is (calling self.byte_len)
        if line < self->line_starts.len:
            set end is (self->line_starts at line) - 1
        if end > start:
            if (calling self.byte_at with (end - 1)) == SOURCE_CR:
                set end is end - 1
        return end
